Data-egress notice — cloud offload backends (V8-02).

cImp's task-offload feature is local and offline by default: the model,
the agent loop, and the tools all run on your machine. The optional
offload "backend pool" can additionally include a *cloud*
OpenAI-compatible endpoint. When — and only when — you add a backend
marked "cloud" and grant the explicit data-egress consent toggle, and the
router selects that backend for a task, cImp sends that task's
instructions (and any context the calling session passes, plus any tool
results if you widen the backend's tool scope beyond the web/docs-only
default) to that third-party endpoint over the network. By default a cloud
backend is denied the local-data tools (read_file, code_search,
run_command, filesystem, git) and a task that needs them is never routed
to it. LAN/remote backends on your own network keep data on your network.
No cloud egress occurs unless you configure and consent to a cloud
backend. The third-party endpoint's data handling is governed by that
provider, independent of the cImp licenses above.
